+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from`
+into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`; neither argument is mutated. The patch holds only what changed:
+objects are compared member by member, and arrays are aligned on their longest common run of equal
+items, so an item added to or removed from an array is a single `add` or `remove`, and a moved item is a
+`remove` plus an `add`, without rewriting the items around it. Values of different types, or primitives
+that differ, produce a `replace` (at path `""` for the root). Tests: `npm test`.
